  "lean": {
    "statement": "∀ {E : Type u_1}\n  [inst : MeasurableSpace E] [inst_1 : NormedAddCommGroup E] [inst_2 : InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]\n  [BorelSpace E] (μ : MeasureTheory.Measure E) [MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure μ] (η : ℝ≥0 × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E) → ℝ),\n  Measurable η →\n    ∀ (κ c q Δ γ C : ℝ),\n      1 ≤ κ →\n        0 < c →\n          c < 1 / 4 →\n            (∀ (s : ℝ≥0 × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)), 0 < η s ∧ η s ≤ c) →\n              0 < Module.finrank ℝ E →\n                2 ≤ q →\n                  0 < Δ →\n                    Δ ≤ 1 / 2 →\n                      0 < γ →\n                        γ ≤ 1 →\n                          8 ≤ C →\n                            ∀ (s0 : ℝ≥0 × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E))\n                              (Q Lterm : ProbabilityTheory.Kernel (ℝ≥0 × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)) E)\n                              [ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel Q] [ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel Lterm],\n                              have K := fun r => (1 + r) / (κ⁻¹ + r);\n                              have τ := fun r => if 2 ≤ K r then K r else c;\n                              have a := fun s => (η s + τ ↑s.1) / (1 + ↑s.1);\n                              have L := q + Real.log (K ↑s0.1 * ↑(Module.finrank ℝ E) * q / Δ);\n                              have B := γ / (√(↑(Module.finrank ℝ E) * L) + L);\n                              have J := ⌈C * Real.log (Real.exp 1 * K ↑s0.1 / B)⌉₊;\n                              ∃ F P R,\n                                (∀ (s : ℝ≥0 × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)) (y : E),\n                                    ↑(F (s, y)).1 = ↑s.1 + (a s)⁻¹ ∧\n                                      (F (s, y)).2 =\n                                        ((↑s.1 + (a s)⁻¹)⁻¹ • (↑s.1 • s.2.1 + (a s)⁻¹ • y), s.2.2.1 + 1, fun n =>\n                                          Nat.casesOn n y s.2.2.2)) ∧\n                                  ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel P ∧\n                                    (∀ (n : ℕ), ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel (R n)) ∧\n                                      (∀ (s : ℝ≥0 × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)),\n                                          P s =\n                                            if B⁻¹ ≤ ↑s.1 then MeasureTheory.Measure.dirac s\n                                            else MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun y => F (s, y)) (Q s)) ∧\n                                        (∀ (n : ℕ), R n = Lterm ∘ₖ (P ^ n)) ∧\n                                          0 < B ∧\n                                            ((P ^ J) s0) {s | B⁻¹ ≤ ↑s.1} = 1 ∧\n                                              (∀ (m : ℕ), (R (J + m)) s0 = (R J) s0) ∧\n                                                ↑J ≤ (3 * C + C / 2 * Real.log (1 / γ)) * L",
    "statement_sha256": "f8accd7626b16c62525db43f85ee4c0fdac05e176ba3f51e067d5e7fcc25f87f",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "Measure E is a countably additive measure. IsProbabilityMeasure means mass one. Kernel X Y is a measurable assignment of measures on Y to X; IsMarkovKernel means each fiber has mass one.",
      "The state is the right-associated product NNReal times E times Nat times (Nat to E), with product measurable structures. For s=(b,u,k,h), s.1=b, s.2.1=u, s.2.2.1=k and s.2.2.2=h. Nat.casesOn n y h equals y at zero and h(m) when n=m+1.",
      "Module.finrank R E is the dimension of E as an R vector space. Real.log is the natural logarithm; Real.exp 1 is e; Nat.ceil is the nonnegative integer ceiling; real casts of naturals and NNReal are used explicitly.",
      "Measure.dirac s is the point mass at s, and Measure.map f mu is pushforward. A kernel evaluated at s and then a measurable set is the mass of that set under its fiber.",
      "Kernel composition L circle_k P first applies P and then L. P^0 is the identity kernel and P^n composes n copies of P. Equality R n = L composed with P^n is equality of entire kernels, whereas equality R(J+m)(s0)=R(J)(s0) concerns only the displayed initial-state fibers."
    ]
  },
